            <ArticleTitle>Arterial blood pressure differences between AutoPulse™ and Lucas2™ during mechanic cardiopulmonary resuscitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13049-016-0253-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 39-year-old patient under constant mechanical CPR with an arterial line in place. The use of AutoPulse™ resulted in higher arterial pressures than the use of LUCAS2™.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
